::: {.doc-subject}

Scaled Schoenfeld residual plots for assessing proportional hazards.
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/greenwood/blob/feat-turnbull-estimator/greenwood/viz/_schoenfeld.py#L67-L172){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
viz.plot_schoenfeld(
    cox,
    *,
    transform="identity",
    show_zph=True,
    title=None,
    backend="altair",
    width=280,
    height=200
)
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Plots scaled Schoenfeld residuals against event time, one panel per covariate, with a loess
smooth line and a dashed reference line at the overall coefficient estimate. Under proportional
hazards, the smooth should be approximately flat. A trend indicates that the covariate's effect
changes over time.

This is the visual equivalent of R's `plot(cox.zph(fit))`.
:::

## Parameters {.doc-parameters}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code>[cox]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Any]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A fitted `CoxPH` model.

<code>[transform]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;identity&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Time-axis transformation: `"identity"` (default), `"log"`, `"km"` (Kaplan-Meier failure
    probability), or `"rank"`.

<code>[show_zph]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   If `True` (default), annotate each panel with the Grambsch-Therneau test p-value from
    `cox_zph()`.

<code>[title]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Optional supertitle for the combined chart.

<code>[backend]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Literal[[&quot;altair&quot;]{.st}, [&quot;plotnine&quot;]{.st}]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;altair&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Plotting backend: `"altair"` (default) or `"plotnine"`.

<code>[width]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[280]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Width of each panel in pixels (Altair) or approximate inches × 72 (plotnine).

<code>[height]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[200]{.dv}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>

:   Height of each panel in pixels (Altair) or approximate inches × 72 (plotnine).
:::

## Returns {.doc-returns}

::: {.doc-definition-items}
<code> [alt.Chart or plotnine.ggplot]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>

:   A composite chart (Altair `HConcatChart`) or a faceted plotnine plot.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}

::: {#5eb9060d .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import greenwood as gw

lung = gw.load_dataset("lung", backend="polars")
y = gw.Surv.right(lung["time"], event=(lung["status"] == 2))
cox = gw.CoxPH().fit(y, lung[["age", "sex"]])

gw.plot_schoenfeld(cox)
```

